1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,900
In Spain the appointment is ten minutes and the paperwork is a folder.

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:08,900
Some of it is unreadable. A guessed dose is worse than none.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:13,900
Anteroom turns that folder into one structured brief.

4
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:20,900
Pick the pages from your library, or photograph them. They upload to your account.

5
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:26,900
Gemini Flash types each document. One tap overrides it.

6
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:31,900
Gemini 2.5 Pro reads both pages, in the EU.

7
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:39,900
It found seven medications. And it refused to guess the eighth.

8
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:45,900
Every other drug has its dose, verbatim. Warfarin has none.

9
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:50,900
Tap the flag, and the original page is right there.

10
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:56,900
Export a PDF for the clinic. On the free tier, the server watermarks it.

11
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:06,900
Anteroom Pro runs on RevenueCat. Buy it, and the app unlocks the moment the entitlement lands.

12
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:12,900
Pro removes the watermark and renders the brief in Spanish.

13
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:17,900
The server decides. The app cannot unlock itself.

14
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:25,900
One Kotlin codebase. Live on iOS today. Try it on TestFlight.

